  = help: `legend` takes a Plot first; `x.legend(...)` is `legend(x, ...)`

== a_legend_with_no_room_for_the_panel
note: 245 rows with NA in educ, wage or hours dropped (line 4)
note: `industry` has 12 categories and the palette 8 colours, so the colours repeat from the ninth category (line 4)
error[Z0401]: a page of 89 by 66 mm is too small for this plot: its labels, never set below 8 points, leave 67.6 by 0.5 mm for the panel
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:1
  |
4 | export(w.plot(x: educ, y: wage, color: industry, size: hours).points().legend(bottom), "small.svg")
  | ^^^^^^ too small a page
  |
  = help: a panel needs 12.7 mm each way; give a larger `size:`, as `one_column` (89 by 66 mm) or `two_column` (183 by 110 mm), or shorten the labels
